WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:07.500
You need 6 to 10 earthworms from your yard, a baking tray, paper towels, a cup of

2
00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.860
plain water, and cardboard to cover the tray.

3
00:00:10.683 --> 00:00:12.243
Line the tray with paper towels.

4
00:00:12.703 --> 00:00:16.543
Wet one half until damp, not puddled, and leave the other half dry.

5
00:00:17.003 --> 00:00:18.183
Cover the tray with cardboard.

6
00:00:18.823 --> 00:00:20.003
Lay the worms across the middle.

7
00:00:20.867 --> 00:00:21.867
Cover the tray again.

8
00:00:22.127 --> 00:00:24.967
Wait 10 minutes, then count the worms on each side.

9
00:00:25.447 --> 00:00:28.847
Expect most worms to end up on the damp side, but not every worm.

10
00:00:29.267 --> 00:00:30.307
Some barely move.

11
00:00:31.050 --> 00:00:32.890
Stay with your child the whole time.

12
00:00:33.290 --> 00:00:36.950
You lift any log or rock, and children stand back about six feet.

13
00:00:37.390 --> 00:00:39.510
Look at, but never touch, any snake.
